  "body": "A stock copied from an incomplete model (#1610) now keeps naming that model's hole after the model is deleted. Before this change, its refusal at the post fell back to \"saved before CamCraft recorded mesh fidelity (project v58 or older)\". The post still refused it; only the reason given was wrong.\n\nFixes #1700\n\n## What changed\n\nThe copy's refusal read the hole from the source model by name (`mesh_open::unknown_note`), so once the source was gone the lookup found nothing. Now the copy carries the hole itself (`schema::MeshOpen`), beside the fidelity-unknown sentinel it already carried (#1056):\n\n- **Where the hole is copied:** every place that lands the sentinel on a copy now lands the hole with it:\n  - `SetStock` and its undo\n  - a setup clone (`CreateSetup` with a datum)\n  - an undone `DeleteSetup`\n  - `UpdateModel`'s refresh of the copies, and its undo\n  - the project loader\n- **Where the refusal reads it:** `model_fidelity::op_problem` reads the hole off the entity that carries the sentinel. Two small helpers: `mesh_open::hole_behind` (the twin of `model_fidelity::chord_behind`) and `mesh_open::note_for`.\n- **Project file:** the saver already wrote `mesh_open` for any entity that has one. The loader now also accepts it on a `FromModel` stock marked `fidelity_unknown`, and a hole without the mark stays corrupt. There is no version bump: #1610's check (a hole on anything but a model is corrupt) has not shipped in a cut yet, so no released reader refuses these files.\n\nThe decisions are recorded in `docs/decisions/1700-stock-copy-hole.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\n- **New:** `crates/app/tests/stock_copy_hole.rs` (6 tests). A copy carries the hole, and its refusal names the source and the hole:\n  - after the source is deleted, and across undo and redo of that delete;\n  - after save, load, and a second save that matches byte for byte;\n  - through a setup clone and an undone setup delete;\n  - through a whole re-import of the source (which clears it) and that re-import's undo;\n  - through `SetStock`'s undo.\n\n  The file also checks that a stock with a hole and no mark fails to load as corrupt.\n- **Without the fix,** the two \"source deleted\" tests fail: the refusal reads \"saved before CamCraft recorded …\".\n- **Existing tests:** the `import_step_open_shell` tests from #1610 still pass. Its corrupt-file message check passes too, because the new message keeps the old wording as a prefix.\n- **Gate:** `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` is green (112 app suites), and `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests -- -D warnings` is clean.\n\nBranched from upstream/main after #1699 merged, not from a cut tag: the code this fixes is not in v0.20.0.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
